{
  "origin": "Traceability used to trace product content alone: a mechanism the plan invented was explicitly out of its reach — `where it leaves the how open, the plan's call stands` — so twelve cycles of Portal's plan review found defects in mechanism the plan had made up and prescribed more of it, one escalation at a time. The standard now covers any mechanism the specification does not decide, and the fix is removal, never justification and never a swap. This walks that on a task whose Do carries a retry schedule, a delivery key and an eviction window nobody decided: the removal is applied, the decided behaviour is restated as criteria, and no replacement mechanism goes in. A real gap in the same file walks beside it, so the removal has to be a judgement about provenance rather than a distrust of the whole tracking file.",
